<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">18092026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Washington has cleared the sale of forty-eight F-thirty-five fighters to Saudi Arabia, a twenty-four billion dollar deal approved despite a United States law that obliges it to preserve Israel's military edge.</s> <s>Export versions of the jet run on mission-data files written in an American laboratory, so the aircraft only sees what Washington allows it to see.</s> <s>Riyadh is buying the most advanced fighter in the region... and the code that makes it work stays with the seller.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Poland's prime minister, Donald Tusk, told parliament that intelligence assessments point to Russian drone and missile strikes on the countries supplying Ukraine, presented as deliberate acts dressed up as accidents.</s> <s>He's describing an assessment, not an incident, and the alliance's answer is less automatic than most assume — NATO's Article Five obliges consultation and whatever action each member deems necessary, individually.</s> <s>A long-range attack drone costs a small fraction of the interceptor fired at it, which is the arithmetic that makes the threat credible, and Tusk travels to Kyiv today to talk about air defence.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Ecuador has jailed José Serrano, once the country's most powerful interior minister, arrested the moment his plane touched down at Santa Elena.</s> <s>He wasn't extradited — he was deported on immigration grounds, and the difference is the whole story, because extradition involves a judge, a specified charge and a rule limiting what he can be tried for, while removal involves none of that.</s> <s>Serrano faces charges connected to the assassination of a presidential candidate, and a case that begins with an aeroplane instead of a warrant is a case that can be undone on appeal.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A court in Aleppo has sentenced a defendant to life imprisonment, the first verdict anywhere for Syria's coastal massacres of March last year, in which more than fourteen hundred people were killed.</s> <s>Sixteen men stood trial, half accused over the rebellion itself and half, mostly soldiers, for violence against Alawite civilians in the villages along the coast.</s> <s>One conviction against fourteen hundred deaths is where accountability begins, not where it ends.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The <sub alias="United Nations">UN</sub> Secretary-General has called for accountability in Sudan without naming any of the states arming the war.</s> <s>Only a panel of experts investigates those weapons flows, it has no enforcement power, and no forum exists that could act on what it finds.</s> <s>A drone killed thirteen civilians in South Kordofan last week, and just forty-two percent of Sudan's humanitarian appeal is funded.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Aswan, Nubian farmers were told no permits remained for the Lake Nasser shoreline, while other farmers worked the very same ground.</s> <s>Egypt's constitution, written in twenty-fourteen, promised Nubians displaced by the Aswan High Dam a right of return — with a deadline that has now quietly passed.</s> <s>Organizers have called a mobilization conference, and half a century after the water rose, the question is whether a constitutional promise means anything once its clock runs out.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Saudi Arabia has again capped Nigeria's Hajj allocation at fifty thousand pilgrims, unchanged despite years of climbing demand from the country with one of the largest Muslim populations on earth.</s> <s>Riyadh sets a global ceiling based on the physical capacity of the sites, divides it among countries, and Nigeria then splits its share again among thirty-six states.</s> <s>Nigerian officials say they'll keep pressing, and for hundreds of thousands of families the pilgrimage remains a queue rather than a plan.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Brazil has raised Bolsa Família payments by fifteen percent, by decree, three weeks before Lula faces Flávio Bolsonaro in an election the polls call a tie.</s> <s>The planning ministry argues inflation since March had already eaten that much, which would make this a restoration rather than new spending — and Brazilian electoral law restricts expanding benefits during a campaign precisely to stop incumbents buying votes.</s> <s>Cash transfers modelled on this programme now run from Indonesia to Pakistan, and every one of them lives in the same tension between a payment large enough to matter and a rule designed to stop politicians competing on generosity.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Bank of Japan has taken its policy rate to one and a quarter percent, the highest in thirty-one years.</s> <s>An entire generation of global finance was built on borrowing yen at almost nothing and buying higher-yielding assets somewhere else — Brazilian rates, Turkish rates, American bonds — and unwinding those positions means selling those assets and buying yen back, everywhere at once.</s> <s>Yet the yen still fell, to one hundred fifty-six per dollar, which tells you markets read this hike as not nearly enough.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India ends a decade of free digital payments on the fifteenth of October, when small merchants begin paying a fee of four tenths of one percent on <sub alias="U P I">UPI</sub> transactions.</s> <s>The charge applies above two thousand rupees and is capped at three hundred, with person-to-person transfers left untouched, but retailers warn it will simply push small traders back to cash.</s> <s>India's payments network moves more transactions than any other on earth, and it's about to find out how much of that volume was built on the word free.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Pakistan, petrol pumps refused to honour a new fuel subsidy on its first day, leaving drivers without the hundred-rupee discount the government had promised.</s> <s>Dealers said they simply lacked the system to process it — the scheme is app-based, and it asks stations to front the money while the central bank promises repayment within forty-eight hours.</s> <s>Islamabad says the funds are earmarked, though a subsidy that depends on a shopkeeper's trust in the state is only as good as the last repayment.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A cat handed to a Bolivian sanctuary ten years ago as an odd-looking stray has turned out to be a species new to science — Leopardus tilcayo, the first new cat described in a century.</s> <s>Naming it took genomic comparisons across thirty-eight feline species, which placed this lineage as splitting from its relatives roughly one point four million years ago.</s> <s>Conservation law runs on names — no Red List assessment, no protected schedule, nothing — so an animal that isn't described is an animal that can't be protected, and this one was described last week.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesia has called off the search for photojournalists who vanished covering the eruption at Anak Krakatau, among them a photographer working for Turkey's Anadolu Agency.</s> <s>That volcano's real danger has never been ash but collapse — in December twenty-eighteen part of its flank slid into the sea and drowned more than four hundred people along the Sunda Strait, with no warning at all, because a landslide wave sends no seismic signal ahead of it.</s> <s>Someone authorised that boat, and the newsrooms that commission a picture from an exclusion zone decide who takes the risk and who carries the insurance.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers writing in Nature have proposed turning the eye into an instrument for psychiatry, the one branch of medicine with no biological test of any kind.</s> <s>Clinicians have read disease in the retina since the eighteen hundreds, and the reason is embryological — the retina is brain tissue, its vessels and neurons tracking vascular, metabolic and neurological change elsewhere in the nervous system.</s> <s>Eye cameras already sit in clinics across South Asia, the Gulf and Africa in numbers psychiatrists in those countries can only envy, though whether any signal separates one patient from another, rather than one group average from another, is still unproven.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Court filings have surfaced internal documents in which Microsoft's own executives describe the training of large language models as an astonishing theft of unprecedented proportions.</s> <s>Another internal memo spells out the loop — search traffic was the payment publishers received for the text that trained these systems, assistants that answer without sending a visitor keep the input and remove the payment, and the next model trains on a thinner, increasingly machine-written web.</s> <s>Languages with the smallest web presence lose most, because a small corpus that stops being written doesn't shrink, it disappears.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>China is running machine-learning forecasting across the largest wind and solar fleet on the planet, and its own engineers describe the technology as no magic bullet.</s> <s>Sharper forecasts genuinely cut the reserve power an operator must hold spinning, which is real money saved — but a prediction is only useful if the grid can act on it, and without transmission lines, storage, or a market that clears quickly, a better forecast just tells you more precisely what you're about to waste.</s> <s>Southeast Asia's utilities are being urged to copy the software, which is the cheapest part of a grid upgrade and by far the easiest to announce.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>